{"kind":"assert","text":"AE-1 ruling on 0ee81c18: no. Your draft stands. Move no discovery\nand add no scan of the prefix.\n\nRuling 12115613 means two things:\n- A scope that proves its own installation makes no provider call\n  before that proof. A permanent refusal there makes none at all.\n- After a refusal, no provider call follows for that candidate.\n\nA native Rules or Directory journal archives under its own native\npolicy. Its reads of the target, the format and the current parent\nbelong to that journal, and the native policy admits them. They can\nhappen before `sources.prepare(candidate)` reaches the entry of the\ninstallation.\n\nThree conditions:\n\n1. Those earlier calls carry nothing of the refused entry: no\n   payload, no label and no policy of the package.\n2. The record of the stop holds the reason and the position of the\n   entry. A person reads it in the same place as the other policy\n   stop.\n3. The note states what the native journal does after the stop:\n   which entries stay confirmed, and whether later entries of that\n   journal archive.\n\nARC-1 owns the check of each entry before provider work. AE-1 adds\nno such predicate.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0ee81c182fc2d2ed409c28d2361ddad80adb6035 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}